\f0\fs26 \cf0 In the great game of cosmic systems theory, one can never be sure if a random event might set up a balancing cycle or a snowball cycle. It depends on the enclosing cycle, the wheels within wheels, whether the wider system snuffs out the effects of a random event or completely collapses around it. This all presupposes that random events exist at all and, as to their role is systems theory, academia is divided. However, if one was to follow the money, one would discover most universities award the richest research grants based on the most advanced evidence-based methodology, which is usually about as reliable\'97despite all the fancy modelling in spreadsheets ten-deep\'97as a coin toss.}